  "question": {
    ":question/id": "90e801a7-dcf3-5468-abc8-4b8dd458dc1a",
    ":question/problem": "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $AB.$",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-6=6\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -36 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-36=6\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -36 \\\\ 1 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,1=(-1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -36 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,6=(-1)\\cdot (-6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -36 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$",
